ademic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Home About Section Menu Dean's Welcome , (current page) Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Dean's Welcome Welcome to the new website for the Office of the Dean of the Faculty at Princeton University! Princeton University’s academic mission is actualized by a distinguished community of scholars that advances knowledge both for its own sake and as a mechanism to inspire the next generation. Our office is charged with ensuring the success and well-being of the faculty, professional researchers, professional specialists, and professional librarians who work at Princeton — and as a team charged with upholding the University’s mission, that responsibility motivates us in all that we do. As an accessible, deliberative partner that is invested in the groundbreaking achievements of Princeton’s academic units and the talented individuals whose scholarly pursuits lead them to Princeton, we aim to respond to the ongoing interests, concerns, and needs of all of our scholars, teachers, and researchers appointed through our office. With a big-picture view of the University's priorities and a deep understanding of its long-term strategic framework, we also work hand-in-hand with the many academic and administrative offices at Princeton in order to support the life and work of our colleagues. Princeton is a place where ideas with global implications take root, and that is central to what makes this an incredible place to work. It is also a foundation from which people with a wide range of life experiences and backgrounds build profound careers. Our updated website provides helpful information about our policies and procedures, but more importantly, it offers a glimpse into the unique texture of our scholarly community. Here you will also find a link to the directory of our staff in the Office of the Dean of the Faculty. At any time, I welcome you to reach out if you need assistance or wish to discuss an idea. As fellow citizens of this incredible University, we believe that partnering to create possibility is our greatest calling. Gene A. Jarrett Dean of the Faculty and William S. Tod Professor of English Related links \"The Enduring Value of the Humanities,\" Princeton Alumni Weekly – May 2024 Link is external Remarks at the 1746 Society Reunions Seminar – May 28, 2023 Link is external The Daily Princetonian Interview – May 8, 2023 Link is external Remarks for the inaugural Distinguished Faculty Service Award – Feb. 6, 2025 \"Defunding the NEH threatens more than just the humanities,\" The Hill – May 10,… Link is external \"Don't laugh: A humanities degree is a smart investment,\" Philadelphia Inquirer… Link is external Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
