ers in specific fields, Princeton University fellowships contribute to the ongoing cultivation of a dynamic community defined by thoughtful and vigorous intellectual exchange. Fellowships Aaron Lemonick Faculty Fellowship in the Council on Science and Technology Established in honor of Aaron Lemonick, Dean of the Faculty from 1973 to 1989, to be awarded to members of the faculty in order that they may develop instructional material, course improvements or new courses that advance the scientific education of non-science students. Year(s) Name of Recipient Department 1990 - 1991 J. Grey Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Bain-Swiggett Lectureship in Poetry (1962) Endowed by the bequest of Glen L. and Emma Bain-Swiggett for the support of an annual visiting lectureship in poetry. Year(s) Name of Recipient 1966 - 1976 R. Whittemore II 1969 - 1970 T. Gunn 1970 - 1971 R. Howard 1971 - 1972 J. P. Creagh 1972 - 1973 M. Strand 1975 - 1976 D. Justice 1978 - 1979 W. Meredith 1984 - 1985 C. Urdang 1984 - 1985 D. Finkel 1986 - 1987 P. Hadas 1989 - 1990 G. Stern 1994 - 1995 D. Donoghue 2008 - 2009 W. Koestenbaum 2010 - 2011 M. N. McLane 2011 - 2012 C. K. Bernstein 2012 - 2013 R. Warren Behrman Senior Fellow in the Humanities (1990) Year(s) Name of Recipient Department 1990 - 1994 W. C. Jordan History 1994 - 1995 A. Grafton History 1995 - 1999 R. Martin Classics 1999 - 2002 L. Engelstein History 2002 - 2006 P. G. Lake History 2002 - 2006 N. Smith English Behrman/Perkins Junior Fellow in the Humanities (1990) Year(s) Name of Recipient 1990 - 1991 F. Ordiway 1991 - 1992 M. Francus 1992 - 1993 D. H. Thurn 1993 - 1994 D. H. Thurn 1994 - 1995 M. Sugrue 1995 - 1996 M. Sugrue 1996 - 1997 G. Strand 1997 - 1998 G. Strand Charles John Gwinn and Alfred Hodder Memorial Fellowship (1941) Year(s) Name of Recipient Department 1944 Richard P. Blackmur 1946 William Aydelotte 1948 Joseph C. Sloane, Jr. 1950 John Berryman 1952 Richard W. B. Lewis 1954 Richard T. Burgi 1955 Peter J. Gay 1957 Joseph