osure Form Academic Professionals Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Section Menu Dean's Welcome Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching , (current page) Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Princeton's visiting professorships for distinguished teaching were established by President Harold T. Shapiro as part of a set of teaching initiatives announced at the beginning of the University's 250th anniversary celebration in 1996. Visitors are selected for their demonstrated teaching excellence and their capacity to bring new ideas in undergraduate teaching to the campus. Each teaches an undergraduate course and engages in other activities to enhance education at Princeton, such as workshops for faculty and graduate students, demonstration lectures and classroom visits. Visitors are invited to introduce new courses and other pedagogic innovations that address significant curricular gaps at the University. Awards Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship for Distinguished Teaching (2000) Established by Laurance S. Rockefeller, Class of 1932, during the Anniversary Campaign for Princeton, to support a distinguished visiting professor at the University Center for Human Values. Visit the University Center for Human Values website Link is external for more information. Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship for Distinguished Teaching (2001) Established by an anonymous alum during the Anniversary Campaign for Princeton, in honor of Stanley Kelley, Jr., Professor of Politics, Emeritus. Visit the nomination page for more information. William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship for Distinguished Teaching (2002) Established by the William R. Kenan, Jr. Charitable Trust to support a distinguished teaching professor in the School of Engineering and Applied Science. Visit the Princeton Engineering website Link is external for more information. 2025–26 Recipients Anita Allen Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship Danielle Lindemann Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship Ellen Eischen William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Jinkyu “JK” Yang William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Nadera Shalhoub-Kevorkian Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship José Torero William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship 2024–25 Recipients Lucas Bessire Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship Gauri Viswanathan Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship Eva Kanso William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Craig Calhoun Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship Rahul Sagar Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship 2023–24 Recipients William Arnold William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Stefano Gonella William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Tad Hirsch William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Rotem Oshman William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Marion Fourcade Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship Wojciech Sadurski Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship 2022–23 Recipients Sindre Bangstad Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship Craig Calhoun Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship R.R.R. (Bert) Smith Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship Francesco Grasso William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Tirza Routtenberg William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Shimon Schocken William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Alison McQueen Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship 2021–22 Recipients John Butt Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship RaMell Ross Stanley Kelley, Jr., Visiting Professorship Harry Van den Akker William R. Kenan, Jr., Visiting Professorship Pratap Mehta Laurance S. Rockefeller Visiting Professorship Previous VPDT Recipients 2020–21 Javier Hidalgo – Rockefeller Christia Mercer – Rockefeller 2019–20 Galia Avidan – Kelley Donka Farkas – Kelley Anne Marie Rasmussen – Kelley Dominik Weiss – Kenan Stephen Stich – Rockefeller 2018–19 Nancy Lape – Kenan Benjamin Berger – Rockefeller 2017–18 Roseanne Ford – Kenan Luis Gonzalez – Kenan Lori Gruen – Rockefeller John Hall – Rockefeller Adam Potkay – Rockefeller 2016–17 Henry Yu – Kelley Eden Fisher – Kenan Susan Brison – Rockefeller 2015–16 Rhonda Garelick – Kelley Keith Devlin – Kelley Geoffrey Sayre-McCord – Rockefeller 2014–15 Heather Love – Kelley Ignacio Paya-Zaforteza – Kenan Dan Edelstein – Rockefeller 2013–14 Keith Devlin – Kelley Andrew Riggsby – Kelley William George – Kenan Deborah Nolan – Kenan Quentin Skinner – Rockefeller 2012–13 Daniel Giammar –