Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Home Governance Section Menu Rules & Procedures Policy Resources Memos Faculty Committees Faculty Meetings , (current page) Faculty Meetings Submenu Faculty Meetings Faculty Meeting Voting Instructions Faculty Referenda Board of Trustees Reporting Terms & Definitions Faculty Meetings As specified by Rules & Procedures of the Faculty , the University faculty meets regularly during the academic year. The first meeting is on the Monday following Labor Day in September, and subsequent meetings are scheduled for the first Monday of every month during the academic year with the following exceptions: (i) if a meeting falls in recess, then the faculty meets on the first Monday after the recess; (ii) unless the faculty votes otherwise at its September and December meetings, no regular meeting is held in October or January, respectively; (iii) the May meeting will be held in late April, and the June meeting will be held in May. The regular hour of meeting is 4:30 p.m. and the regular location is the Faculty Room in Nassau Hall, but the presiding officer, in consultation with the clerk of the faculty, may call the meeting for any hour and location which in their judgment seems desirable. All important proposals should be delivered in writing to the clerk not later than noon on the second Wednesday preceding the meeting at which they shall be introduced, and the clerk shall normally cause such proposals to be printed and distributed to the members of the faculty, to be made public and placed on file, and to be placed in the Order of Business for that meeting, provided that no such proposal offered by an individual member shall be so treated unless it is seconded by another member. Voting Eligibility Rules & Procedures of the Faculty (II.C.1) identifies members of the voting faculty, as follows: “The tenured faculty consist of the Professors and tenured Associate Professors, and the tenure-track faculty consist of the non-tenured Associate Professors and Assistant Professors. The Lecturer Ranks consist of the University Lecturers, Professors of the Practice, Senior Lecturers, Lecturers, Instructors, Lecturers with the Rank of Professor, and Lecturers with the Rank of Associate Professor. The Faculty consists of the President, the Academic Officers, the tenured and tenure-track faculty, and the Lecturer Ranks. The President, the Academic Officers, the tenured and tenure-track faculty, and full-time members of the Lecturer Ranks are entitled to vote at meetings of the Faculty and in any circumstances where votes of the Faculty are taken. The University Librarian is also a voting member of the Faculty.” For your convenience, the Office of the Dean of the Faculty maintains an online portal to determine voting eligibility Link is external . Upcoming Faculty Meetings Please note that all faculty meetings begin at 4:30 p.m. Meetings are normally held in the Faculty Room at Nassau Hall. Sep 14 Faculty Meeting Sep 23 Faculty Meeting Materials Deadline Oct 5 Faculty Meeting Oct 21 Faculty Meeting Materials Deadline Nov 2 Faculty Meeting Nov 25 Faculty Meeting Materials Deadline Dec 7 Faculty Meeting Dec 30 Faculty Meeting Materials Deadline Jan 11 Faculty Meeting Jan 20 Faculty Meeting Materials Deadline Feb 1 Faculty Meeting Feb 17 Faculty Meeting Materials Deadline View All Faculty Meetings Related links Faculty Meeting Voting Eligibility Tool Link is external Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
