      "description": "Faculty Development and Inclusion | Office of the Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Off screen link: Skip to content Off screen link: Skip to search Main Menu Menu About About Submenu About Dean's Welcome Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Submenu Professorships Preceptorships Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Governance Governance Submenu Governance Rules & Procedures Policy Resources Memos Faculty Committees Faculty Committees Submenu Faculty Committee Elections University Faculty Service Recognition Faculty Meetings Faculty Meetings Submenu Faculty Meeting Voting Instructions Faculty Referenda Board of Trustees Reporting Terms & Definitions Faculty Development and Inclusion , (current page) Faculty Development and Inclusion Submenu Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Search Process Talent Pathway Programs Talent Pathway Programs Submenu Presidential Postdoctoral Research Fellows Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty Faculty Submenu Faculty Incoming Faculty Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement Faculty Benefits Compensation Compensation Submenu Faculty Pay Schedule Elections Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Retirement Submenu Retirement Eligibility Top Five Retirement Questions Retirement Planning Process Faculty Retirement Plans Benefits in Retirement Faculty Forms Faculty Forms Submenu Faculty Committee Nomination Form Faculty Leave Request Form Moving Expense Form Request Research Assistance (UCHRSS) Update Personal Information Nepotism Policy Disclosure Form Academic Professionals Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Faculty Development and Inclusion Princeton University is a place where the world’s most inspired teachers and scholars meet. As a University dedicated to excellence, we cultivate an educational environment defined by purpose. Here, individuals with a diverse array of backgrounds, perspectives and experiences find unique opportunities to advance their academic passions while working in concert with their peers and the broader Princeton community to infuse our campus with a sense of possibility. More than a place to work, this is a place to imagine what comes next. Faculty Search Process Princeton's robust faculty search process attracts dynamic global scholars with a passion for big ideas. Talent Pathway Programs We invest meaningfully to identify and support top talent at all stages of their academic careers. Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty and academic professionals engage with award-winning artists and one another in this monthly series. Princeton University is committed to equal opportunity and nondiscrimination To maximize excellence, we seek talent from all segments of American society and the world, and we take steps to ensure everyone at Princeton can thrive while they are here. That is the sole rationale and purpose of our diversity and inclusion programs, all of which are voluntary and open to all, and which comply with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. Princeton does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, disability, or any other protected characteristic, and Princeton does not provide special benefits or preferential treatment on the basis of a protected characteristic. Inclusion Highlights Faculty Diversity Salons to bring renowned literary voices to campus this fall Link is external A new interactive campus map to help you find your way Link is external Link is external Inclusive Princeton report spotlights programs and initiatives that support vibrant campus community Link is external Resources Faculty Advisory Committee on Diversity Meet the members of our Faculty Advisory Committee on Diversity . They advise the President, Provost, and Dean of the Faculty on issues and initiatives relating to diversity and inclusion, including faculty hiring, policies, curriculum, and campus climate. Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Annual Report Princeton University’s annual report on diversity, equity, and inclusion Link is external highlights many of the events, initiatives and programs completed during the academic year. The report also features updated demographic and climate survey data. Inclusive Princeton Learn more about Princeton's commitment to diversity and inclusion at Inclusive Princeton Link is external . There, you can connect with resources including campus networks and offices Link is external , employee networks Link is external , and more. Additionally, the site includes policies and resources pertaining to discrimination, harassment, and/or sexual misconduct complaints Link is external . Racial Equity Princeton recognizes that confronting racial inequity Link is external is a journey we must undertake as a community. We encourage members of our community to raise their voices and share their ideas and suggestions as we learn and evolve. Inclusive Reading List & Tools Academic inclusion guides for departments Link is external Gender bias letter of recommendation calculator Link is external, Link opens in new window Gender decoder for Job Ads Link is external, Link opens in new window Implicit Association Test (IAT) Link is external, Link opens in new window Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Toolkits Link is external UCLA’s Implicit Bias Video Series Link is external, Link opens in new window Gender and letters of recommendation for academics Link is external, Link opens in new window Contacts Frederick F. Wherry Vice Dean for Faculty Development and Inclusion Office Phone 609-258-4421 Link opens phone app Email vddevelopment@princeton.edu Rayna Truelove Associate Dean for Faculty Development and Inclusion Office Phone 609-258-7081 Link opens phone app Email truelove@princeton.edu Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
