sionals Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Home Faculty Development and Inclusion Section Menu Faculty Search Process Talent Pathway Programs Faculty Diversity Salons , (current page) Faculty Diversity Salons “Art holds the power to change communities. Through exploring our unique voices, we learn to value and celebrate our differences, and in the process discover our common humanity. That is the amazing power of art.” — Michael McElroy, Chair and Arthur E. and Martha S. Hearron Endowed Professor of Musical Theater, University of Michigan With an emphasis on becoming community, faculty and academic professionals engage with award-winning international artists and one another in this spirited monthly series. Once a month, professors, academic professionals and their families gather to experience the power of art. Engaging with award-winning artists and each other, we are continually becoming community. Watch your inbox for monthly event reminders and registration details. Salons are open to all Office of the Dean of Faculty appointees, without regard to identity or other protected characteristics. Sponsored by the Office of the Dean of Faculty. 2026-27 Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty Diversity Salon: Kevin Young Friday, September 18, 2026 , 5:30 pm Faculty Diversity Salon: Mai Der Vang Friday, October 2, 2026 , 5:30 pm Faculty Diversity Salon: Marcelo Hernandez Castillo Friday, November 13, 2026 , 5:30 pm Faculty Diversity Salon: LaTasha N. Nevada Diggs Friday, January 29, 2027 , 5:30 pm Faculty Diversity Salon: Nikky Finney Friday, February 26, 2027 , 5:30 pm Faculty Diversity Salon: Li-Young Lee Friday, March 26, 2027 , 5:30 pm Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
