    "http://dof.princeton.edu/faculty/incoming-faculty": {
      "title": "Office of the Dean of the Faculty",
      "description": "Incoming Faculty | Office of the Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Off screen link: Skip to content Off screen link: Skip to search Main Menu Menu About About Submenu About Dean's Welcome Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Submenu Professorships Preceptorships Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Governance Governance Submenu Governance Rules & Procedures Policy Resources Memos Faculty Committees Faculty Committees Submenu Faculty Committee Elections University Faculty Service Recognition Faculty Meetings Faculty Meetings Submenu Faculty Meeting Voting Instructions Faculty Referenda Board of Trustees Reporting Terms & Definitions Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Development and Inclusion Submenu Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Search Process Talent Pathway Programs Talent Pathway Programs Submenu Presidential Postdoctoral Research Fellows Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty , (current section) Faculty Submenu Faculty Incoming Faculty , (current page) Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement Faculty Benefits Compensation Compensation Submenu Faculty Pay Schedule Elections Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Retirement Submenu Retirement Eligibility Top Five Retirement Questions Retirement Planning Process Faculty Retirement Plans Benefits in Retirement Faculty Forms Faculty Forms Submenu Faculty Committee Nomination Form Faculty Leave Request Form Moving Expense Form Request Research Assistance (UCHRSS) Update Personal Information Nepotism Policy Disclosure Form Academic Professionals Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Home Resources for Faculty Section Menu Incoming Faculty , (current page) Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement Faculty Benefits Compensation Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Forms Incoming Faculty Prepare to advance your work in a community of scholars defined by excellence. As an incoming member of the faculty at Princeton University, you have joined a unique community of passionate educators and researchers. To make the onboarding process straightforward, we have collected key resources here. Have questions? We are always available to assist you, both now and in the future. The Onboarding Process Contact Your Home Department First things first, coordinate your arrival with your home department. In addition to the steps outlined here, they may have additional onboarding processes for you to complete. View an updated list of departmental contacts . Complete the I-9 Employment Eligibility Process As required by law, employees working in the United States are required to complete the I-9 process at the time of hire, rehire or when their work authorization documents expire. New employees are required to complete Section 1 of the I-9 on or before the employee’s first day of employment . Section 2 must be completed within three business days of the employee’s first day of employment . Human Resources representatives will be available on campus to conduct the I-9 process for all employees (casuals, staff, DOF appointees) per the following schedule. Days: Mondays and Thursdays Location: New South Building, Room B10 Time: 9 a.m. to noon (Eastern Standard Time) Hours will be extended from 9 a.m. to 4 p.m. on the following days: Monday, Aug. 31 – New South Building, 7th Floor Training Room Tuesday, Sept. 1 – New South Building, 7th Floor Training Room Thursday, Sept. 3 – New South Building, 7th Floor Training Room There will be no appointments on Monday, Sept. 7 (closed for holiday). There will be special hours from 9 a.m. to noon on Tuesday, Sept. 8. Appointments are encouraged, walk-in appointments are acceptable. Please use HR's I-9 scheduling link Link is external to make an appointment. Employees are sent instructions to their Princeton email account two weeks prior to their start date to complete Section 1 of I-9 in the Tracker online system, along with the details to present their documentation to HR to complete Section 2 of the process. Employees residing within the tri-state region (NJ, PA, NY) are required to complete the I-9 in person. Those who are approved to work fully remote outside of the region, may contact careers@princeton.edu to make alternate arrangements. Access Your Princeton netID and Email Account University accounts are set up for all University faculty and staff, and unlock access to technology services including University email accounts, the campus network, and more. The Office of Information Technology Link is external makes it easy to get started and offers tech support when you need it. Note that other aspects of the onboarding process are explained in important information that will be sent to your University email account. Benefits New Hire Orientation All incoming new hires are invited to attend a special online question and answer webinar about Princeton University benefits. Prior to attending, we invite you to view our Benefits Link is external New Hire Orientation Link is external , which can explain the differences in our plan types and provide more insight in making an election for you and your family. New Hire Informational Videos Link is external New Hire Benefits Booklet 2026 Link downloads document What: Review medical plans, enrollment process and answer questions about plan options. When: (Please choose one session – approximately 90 minutes each ) Monday, August 31, 2026 Link is external Tuesday, September 8, 2026 Link is external Registration: Click on the above selected session or email benefits@princeton.edu or call (609) 258-3302. Include your name and session date to receive Zoom meeting invite for requested date. Get Your TigerCard (University ID) Your TigerCard establishes your affiliation with Princeton University and serves as a photo ID. In addition to serving as an ID, your TigerCard gains you access to: The Library The Athletics Department McCosh Health Center The Housing Office The Frist Campus Center Ticket Office Campus buildings and high security areas that are electronically secured Your TigerCard is also used as a debit card to pay for food or copy services. You may pick up your TigerCard at the TigerCard Office, part of The Service Point Link is external in New South. Contact 609-258-8300 or thepoint@princeton.edu with any questions. Manage Transportation & Parking Parking & Transportation Services offers essential information about getting to and around campus, including vehicle registration for parking permits. Be sure to check out the Revise Your Ride Link is external program, which offers enhanced benefits and incentives to participants in one of five alternate commuter programs: bike/walk, carpool, vanpool, transit reimbursement, or NJ Transit bus pass. Complete the University's Online Preventing Sexual Harassment Training All Princeton University faculty and staff are required to complete the University's online Preventing Sexual Harassment Program Link is external, Link opens in new window within 30 days of the start date. This 45-minute e-learning program provides information about University policies related to sexual harassment, campus resources, and each employee's reporting obligation. For more information, please see the Sexual Misconduct Prevention FAQs Link is external . If you have any questions about the program, email ptitleix@princeton.edu . For technical questions, email training@princeton.edu . Important Notice: Run the course in Edge or Chrome browser. If Firefox is your default browser, copy and paste the course link into Edge or Chrome browser window. HR Self Service Use HR Self Service Link is external, Link opens in new window to update your name, marital status, direct deposit, addresses, contact information, or emergency contacts. Please note that HR Self-Service cannot be accessed prior to the hire date. Selecting Your Computer Find more details Link is external . Establish Your ORCID iD Many external research funders, including federal grantmaking agencies and publishers, now require researchers to establish and maintain an ORCID iD Link is external . This unique identifier not only assists in managing your public scholarly information, but also enhances your visibility within the academic community. More information is available on the Princeton University Library website Link is external and the Office of Research and Project Administration website Link is external . Additional Resources Depending on your needs, the following offices may also be of assistance. Visas: Davis International Center Louis A. Simpson International Building, A-Level 20 Washington Road 609-258-5006 The Davis International Center Link is external is committed to providing services and programs that support your growth, development, and welfare, including immigration regulatory advising and processing, cultural adjustment, social enrichment, and assistance with practical matters related to living in the U.S. They have walk-in hours (no appointment necessary), or you can schedule an appointment. Contact the Davis International Center for assistance with: Visa sponsorship and entering the U.S. Reporting your arrival (including mandatory check-in for J1 Visa holders) Orientation and settling in Tax and Social Security requirements Resources for spouses and families Please note: J-1 Visa Status: You MUST check in within 30 days of your DS-2019 start date or your immigration record will be terminated. Check-in can only be completed online, by appointment, or during designated walk-in hours. Other Visa Holders (e.g., H-1B, F-1 OPT): Schedule an appointment or stop in during walk-in hours to report your arrival. Housing New South Building, 5th floor 609-258-3460 Contact the Housing Office Link is external for information or assistance with University Faculty and Staff Housing, including limited accommodations for postdocs. Requests for Accommodations Princeton University provides reasonable accommodations for employees and individuals to whom a job offer has been made who have a disability. Visit the HR website Link is external to learn more about the University’s policies and accommodation process. Library Services Bring your TigerCard ID card to activate your patron barcode and access the incredible collections housed at the Princeton University libraries Link is external . Campus Recreation Dillon Gymnasium, Room 103 rec@princeton.edu 9 a.m. to 5 p.m., Monday to Friday Princeton takes a broad view of employee wellness, and offers access to numerous recreational opportunities both formal and informal. As a faculty or staff member of Princeton University, you are able to purchase a recreational membership to Dillon Gym at a discounted rate. Visit the Campus Rec website Link is external for details. Dual Career Support Career support is available on a limited basis to spouses and partners of new, senior faculty recruited to Princeton University as they begin to envision their lives in the greater Princeton area. A career transition adviser in the Office of the Dean of the Faculty works closely with partners and spouses of new faculty as they navigate the various challenges that can accompany professional transitions. Services include: Personalized coaching Resume and employment application review Interview preparation Networking support Business plan writing and entrepreneurial advisement Career transition assistance/professional license transfer guidance Continuing education exploration Commuting options Neighborhood and school evaluations Inquiries may be directed to odof-academic@princeton.edu for consideration. Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
    },
    "http://dof.princeton.edu/faculty/faculty-ranks-appointment-advancement": {
      "title": "Office of the Dean of the Faculty",
      "description": "Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement | Office of the Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Off screen link: Skip to content Off screen link: Skip to search Main Menu Menu About About Submenu About Dean's Welcome Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Submenu Professorships Preceptorships Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Governance Governance Submenu Governance Rules & Procedures Policy Resources Memos Faculty Committees Faculty Committees Submenu Faculty Committee Elections University Faculty Service Recognition Faculty Meetings Faculty Meetings Submenu Faculty Meeting Voting Instructions Faculty Referenda Board of Trustees Reporting Terms & Definitions Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Development and Inclusion Submenu Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Search Process Talent Pathway Programs Talent Pathway Programs Submenu Presidential Postdoctoral Research Fellows Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty , (current section) Faculty Submenu Faculty Incoming Faculty Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement , (current page) Faculty Benefits Compensation Compensation Submenu Faculty Pay Schedule Elections Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Retirement Submenu Retirement Eligibility Top Five Retirement Questions Retirement Planning Process Faculty Retirement Plans Benefits in Retirement Faculty Forms Faculty Forms Submenu Faculty Committee Nomination Form Faculty Leave Request Form Moving Expense Form Request Research Assistance (UCHRSS) Update Personal Information Nepotism Policy Disclosure Form Academic Professionals Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Home Resources for Faculty Section Menu Incoming Faculty Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement , (current page) Faculty Benefits Compensation Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Forms Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement Princeton’s research and teaching mission is advanced through visionary scholarship that redefines the bounds of disciplinary knowledge. Elevating the individual within a culture of collaboration, Princeton is a powerful foundation upon which to build one’s career and family. To continually cultivate Princeton University’s unrivaled community of scholars, the Office of the Dean of the Faculty supports academic departments throughout the appointment and advancement process. We also offer insight and guidance as you plan your next steps with clear details on ranks and University advancement criteria for faculty members. Promoting Visionary Careers The appointment and advancement process at Princeton University recognizes the formidable contributions of our faculty not just to teaching and research at the University, but to the ongoing creation of fundamental knowledge and insight of value for its own sake. Here you will find information about traditional pathways within our faculty ranks. Tenured & Tenure-Track Faculty Recommendations for the advancement of ladder faculty are made by the department chair, in consultation with department faculty holding full or joint appointments. For detailed information on these ranks, with advancement criteria, please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, sections IV A-C. RANK APPOINTMENT AND ADVANCEMENT Professor Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV A, Appointment and Advancement of Professors . Associate Professor Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV B, Appointment and Advancement of Associate Professors . Assistant Professor Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV C, Appointment and Advancement of Assistant Professors . Non-Tenure Track Faculty Recommendations for the advancement of non-tenure-track faculty are made by the department chair, in consultation with tenured and tenure-track faculty, along with full-time lecturers and professors of the practice with full or joint appointments in the department. For detailed information on these ranks, with advancement criteria, please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, sections IV D-H. RANK APPOINTMENT AND ADVANCEMENT University Lecturer* Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV D, Appointment and Advancement of University Lecturers . Professor of the Practice* Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV E, Appointment and Advancement of Professors of the Practice . Senior Lecturers Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV F, Appointment and Advancement of Senior Lecturers . Lecturers Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV G, Appointment and Advancement of Lecturers . Instructors Please review Rules & Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University, section IV H, Appointment and Advancement of Instructors . Rules & Procedures Rules and Procedures of the Faculty of Princeton University Policies Equal Opportunity Non-Discrimination Statement Tenure Clock Extension for New Parent s Workload Relief for New Parents Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
    },
