      "description": "Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization | Office of the Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Off screen link: Skip to content Off screen link: Skip to search Main Menu Menu About About Submenu About Dean's Welcome Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Submenu Professorships Preceptorships Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Governance Governance Submenu Governance Rules & Procedures Policy Resources Memos Faculty Committees Faculty Committees Submenu Faculty Committee Elections University Faculty Service Recognition Faculty Meetings Faculty Meetings Submenu Faculty Meeting Voting Instructions Faculty Referenda Board of Trustees Reporting Terms & Definitions Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Development and Inclusion Submenu Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Search Process Talent Pathway Programs Talent Pathway Programs Submenu Presidential Postdoctoral Research Fellows Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty Faculty Submenu Faculty Incoming Faculty Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement Faculty Benefits Compensation Compensation Submenu Faculty Pay Schedule Elections Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Retirement Submenu Retirement Eligibility Top Five Retirement Questions Retirement Planning Process Faculty Retirement Plans Benefits in Retirement Faculty Forms Faculty Forms Submenu Faculty Committee Nomination Form Faculty Leave Request Form Moving Expense Form Request Research Assistance (UCHRSS) Update Personal Information Nepotism Policy Disclosure Form Academic Professionals , (current section) Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization , (current page) Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Home Academic Professionals Section Menu Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization , (current page) Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization A group named Princeton University Postdocs and Scholars (PUPS-UAW) filed a petition on April 2, 2024, with the National Labor Relations Board (NLRB) to hold an election to determine whether postdocs and associate research scholars should be represented by the International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace and Agricultural Implement Workers of America (“United Auto Workers”). In an election held on May 8 and 9, 2024, postdocs and associate research scholars voted in favor of being represented by PUPS-UAW. Princeton University respects the right of employees to unionize. This page will host news and updates regarding negotiations with the bargaining unit. Prior to the 2024 election, the Office of the Dean of the Faculty provided information and resources to postdocs and associate research scholars to make an informed decision about whether or not to choose to be represented by a union. These resources are archived through the associated pages linked below. News Collective Bargaining Updates – May 12, 2026 This update summarizes the 32nd and 33rd bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS‑UAW. During these meetings, the parties continued to exchange responses to proposals on compensation and benefits and continued to dialogue on several noneconomic articles. Collective Bargaining Updates – April 9, 2026 This update summarizes the 30th and 31st bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS‑UAW. During these meetings, the parties exchanged comprehensive responses to proposals on compensation and benefits and continued discussion of several noneconomic articles. Collective Bargaining Updates – March 10, 2026 This update provides information on the 29th bargaining session between the University and PUPS‑UAW, during which the University presented its comprehensive response to the Union’s full economic package, including compensation and benefits. Collective Bargaining Updates – Feb. 12, 2026 This update provides information on the 25th, 26th, 27th and 28th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams (covering sessions in December 2025, January 2026 and February 2026), including the parties coming to two more tentative agreements on substantive provisions of the future contract. Collective Bargaining Updates – Dec. 4, 2025 This update provides information on the 23rd and 24th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on another substantive provision of the future contract during the second session in November. Collective Bargaining Updates – Nov. 7, 2025 This update provides information on the 21st and 22nd bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams. Collective Bargaining Updates – Oct. 7, 2025 This update provides information on the 19th and 20th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on another substantive provision of the future contract during the first session in September. Collective Bargaining Updates – Sept. 4, 2025 This update provides information on the 16th, 17th, and 18th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on three substantive provisions of the future contract during their July session. Collective Bargaining Updates – June 4, 2025 This update provides information on the 14th and 15th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams. Collective Bargaining Updates – May 2, 2025 This update provides information on the 12th and 13th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on another substantive provision of the future collective bargaining agreement during their last scheduled session in April. Collective Bargaining Updates – April 7, 2025 This update provides information on the ninth, 10th and 11th bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on another substantive provision of the future collective bargaining agreement. Collective Bargaining Updates – March 6, 2025 This update provides information on the seventh and eighth bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on another substantive provision of the future collective bargaining agreement. Collective Bargaining Updates – Feb. 5, 2025 This update provides information on the fifth and sixth bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on another substantive provision of the future collective bargaining agreement. Collective Bargaining Updates – Dec. 12, 2024 This update provides information on the first four bargaining sessions between the University and PUPS-UAW bargaining teams, including the parties coming to a tentative agreement on one provision of the future collective bargaining agreement. Postdocs and associate research scholars form union at Princeton In an election held on May 8 and 9, 2024, postdocs and associate research scholars voted in favor of being represented by PUPS-UAW, a union affiliated with the International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace and Agricultural Implement Workers of America (“United Auto Workers”). Postdocs and associate research scholars to vote on unionization May 8-9 An election will be held Wednesday, May 8, and Thursday, May 9, 2024, at Frist Campus Center to decide whether postdoctoral researchers and associate research scholars at Princeton University will form an employee union, represented by the International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace and Agricultural Implement Workers of America. ODoF Communications Regarding Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) about Unionization Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
    },
    "https://postdocs.princeton.edu": {
      "title": "National Postdoc Appreciation Week: View the schedule",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researchers | Office of the Dean of the Faculty Office of the Dean of the Faculty Off screen link: Skip to content Off screen link: Skip to search Main Menu Menu About About Submenu About Dean's Welcome Meet Our Team Whom to Contact Facts & Figures Our History and Past Deans Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Endowed Professorships, Preceptorships & Fellowships Submenu Professorships Preceptorships Fellowships Emeriti Faculty Bios President's Award for Distinguished Teaching Visiting Professorships for Distinguished Teaching Howard T. Behrman Award for Distinguished Achievement in the Humanities Meet The Faculty Public Lectures Link is external Governance Governance Submenu Governance Rules & Procedures Policy Resources Memos Faculty Committees Faculty Committees Submenu Faculty Committee Elections University Faculty Service Recognition Faculty Meetings Faculty Meetings Submenu Faculty Meeting Voting Instructions Faculty Referenda Board of Trustees Reporting Terms & Definitions Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Development and Inclusion Submenu Faculty Development and Inclusion Faculty Search Process Talent Pathway Programs Talent Pathway Programs Submenu Presidential Postdoctoral Research Fellows Faculty Diversity Salons Faculty Faculty Submenu Faculty Incoming Faculty Faculty Ranks, Appointment & Advancement Faculty Benefits Compensation Compensation Submenu Faculty Pay Schedule Elections Learning & Professional Development Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Faculty Retirement Faculty Retirement Submenu Retirement Eligibility Top Five Retirement Questions Retirement Planning Process Faculty Retirement Plans Benefits in Retirement Faculty Forms Faculty Forms Submenu Faculty Committee Nomination Form Faculty Leave Request Form Moving Expense Form Request Research Assistance (UCHRSS) Update Personal Information Nepotism Policy Disclosure Form Academic Professionals Academic Professionals Submenu Academic Professionals Incoming Academic Professionals Benefits for Academic Professionals Academic Professional Career Ranks & Advancement Research for Academic Professionals Professional Development for Academic Professionals Checklist for Departure Link downloads document Information About Postdoc and Associate Research Scholar Unionization Postdoctoral Scholars Link is external Visitors Visitors Submenu Visitors Incoming Visitors Visitor Ranks & Appointments Visitor Benefits Academic Units Academic Units Submenu Academic Units Directory of Academic Units, Chairs, Directors & Managers Guidebook for Chairs, Directors and Managers Guidelines for Academic Reviews Systems Guide & How-To’s Systems Guide & How-To’s Submenu Interfolio Faculty Search Authorization Request Guide AHIRE Guide DOF DropBox Instructions Salary Commitment Guidelines Salary Review Process Guide Faculty Roles Administration Guide New Jersey Pay Transparency Act Forms and Data Submission Forms and Data Submission Submenu Appointment and Promotion Checklists List of Current Systems Helpful Tools Calendar of Major Actions and Important Dates News Benefits Apply FAQs iThenticate FAQs Search Search Postdoctoral Researchers On this page On this page National Postdoc Appreciation Week\n                          : View the schedule Incoming Postdoctoral Researchers Benefits Research Support Professional Development News Events National Postdoc Appreciation Week\n                          : View the schedule Incoming Postdoctoral Researchers Benefits Research Support Professional Development News Events Princeton University has over 700 postdoctoral researchers conducting research in more than 50 departments on campus. The University offers a wealth of programs and resources to help postdoctoral researchers adjust to life at Princeton. Offering pragmatic guidance, the Office of the Dean of the Faculty can help you navigate and leverage the many resources available to you during your time with us. National Postdoc Appreciation Week : View the schedule National Postdoc Appreciation Week is Sept. 21-25. Join the Office of the Dean of the Faculty for a week of community, wellness and celebration! View the schedule What is a Postdoctoral Researcher? A postdoc at Princeton is a researcher who has completed all requirements for their Ph.D., including successfully defending their dissertation. The University supports postdocs through fellowships or training grants as they work to advance their careers. Whether you seek funding opportunities, career development resources, or research collaboration, we are here to help you navigate your postdoctoral journey. Navigate the suite of comprehensive benefits available to Princeton postdocs and contact our assistant dean for postdoctoral affairs with any questions. More information on postdoc terms and ranks Unionization Information Incoming Postdoctoral Researchers Complete the onboarding process and access the many resources available to you at Princeton. Step-by-Step Onboarding Process To help make your welcome to Princeton as comfortable and straightforward as possible, we have collected key steps and resources for easy access. Link is external Visas Link is external Prospective and current Princeton postdocs seeking general information related to J-1, H-1B, TN, O-1 or other employment-based visa statuses or B-1/WB are encouraged to consult our visa resources. Link is external Transportation and Parking Link is external For information about transportation and on-campus parking, see our resources for rail and airport services, local buses and parking instructions. Link is external Housing Link is external Information regarding staff housing, including contacts, rates and application forms, is available. Space is limited. Link is external Off-Campus Housing Link is external Non-University housing options in the Princeton area can be found on the off-campus housing web page. Link is external Revise Your Ride Link is external Save money, spend less time in traffic, and contribute to campus sustainability by leaving your car at home or sharing a ride with a colleague. Benefits Contact the University's Human Resources Department Link is external to explore the comprehensive suite of benefits available to you and your family as a postdoctoral researcher at Princeton. Link is external Wellness Link is external Princeton takes an expansive view of wellness, from physical and mental health to financial planning and tools that facilitate work-life balance for you and your family. Link is external Health Link is external Benefits-eligible employees enjoy comprehensive yet flexible health insurance plans and competitive dental, vision, and prescription drug plans that address individual needs. Mental Wellness Resources Princeton University is dedicated to supporting the well-being of our community, offering comprehensive resources and programs for the betterment of your mental health. Link is external Family Benefits Link is external Princeton offers a comprehensive array of family benefits, including maternity leave and childcare opportunities. Research Support Explore our diverse catalog of research opportunities dedicated to cultivating well-rounded postdoctoral researchers. Link is external Funding Link is external Princeton provides comprehensive external and third-party resources for finding research funding available to academic professionals through the Office of the Dean for Research. Link is external Office of the Dean for Research Link is external The Office of the Dean for Research provides information and guidance across research areas, from collaboration and funding opportunities to research compliance. Internal Research Opportunities The University encourages early career scholars to pursue a career in academia by supporting their postdoctoral work at Princeton through fellowships and internal research grants. Link is external Research and Project Administration Link is external Research and Project Administration provides support and guidance to researchers for obtaining sponsored research funds and managing sponsored program activity in today's complex regulatory environment. Link is external Research Integrity and Assurance Link is external Research Integrity and Assurance provides compliance and regulatory expertise to promote responsible and ethical research practices within the research community. Professional Development Deepen your research and work with a collection of career and learning opportunities. Link is external NCFDD Link is external NCFDD offers professional development, training and mentorship to more than 83,000 members. Offerings include the popular Faculty Success Program Link is external . Create a free account Link is external for on-demand access to mentoring, tools and support. Link is external Employee Learning Center Link is external From department-specific training to courses covering research and the latest digital technologies, the Employee Learning Center offers both targeted and general interest training online. Link is external National Postdoctoral Association (NPA) Link is external The NPA works to empower postdocs through a culture of inclusive connection, and provides a wealth of resources and networking opportunities. Postdocs enjoy free access to an NPA membership. Sign up with your Princeton email. Career Development Support Link is external Developing an IDP Link is external Looking for a resource that helps you map out your career pathway? The American Psychological Association provides the framework for your success through an Individual Development Plan (IDP). Link is external Career Guidance: myIDP Link is external myIDP is a web-based career-planning tool designed to help you identify your career goals in the sciences and develop a step-by-step plan to achieve them. Link is external Career Guidance: ImaginePhD Link is external ImaginePhD is a free online career exploration and planning tool for postdoctoral scholars in the humanities and social sciences. Link sends email Careers Outside of Academia Link sends email Explore careers outside of academia. Define your path, develop an action plan, and more. Email your resume and a brief note regarding your query to Kate Hammond. Teaching Resources Link is external McGraw Center for Teaching and Learning Link is external Access an array of workshops and events, covering everything from working with your adviser or AI to developing your teaching and mentoring skills. Individual learning consultations are also available. Teaching Outside Princeton Teaching at another college or university is an outside activity, external to your Princeton responsibilities. Requests for permission must be submitted to the Office of the Dean of the Faculty. Prospective Postdocs Link is external Interested in an academic position at Princeton? The University strives for the highest levels of quality in research and education as we pursue a mission of service to the nation and world. If you are interested in joining Princeton University's research or teaching community. Each department/program manages recruitment for postdoctoral positions. Review our list of University academic departments , which includes contact information for academic chairs and managers. Note: Effective Jan. 7, 2026, we have transitioned to Interfolio for academic hiring. Most candidates should use the Interfolio link below. Some previously posted open positions remain in our legacy system until Sept. 30, 2026. View Open Academic Positions (Interfolio) Link is external, Link opens in new window View Previously Posted Open Positions (Legacy System) Link is external, Link opens in new window News Link is external Richard Kang Awarded Beckman Fellowship Link is external Link is external Sorting cells’ inner structures provides new path to drug development Link is external Link is external Technique to design peptides creates new hybrid forms Link is external Events Sep 21 Sep\n  21\n\n\n      \n        : NPAW: Fuel Up: Coffee and Bagels Sept. 21, 2026, 10 a.m. Sep 22 Sep\n  22\n\n\n      \n        : NPAW: Postdoc Orientation Sept. 22, 2026, 1 p.m. Sep 23 Sep\n  23\n\n\n      \n        : NPAW: Yoga Session – Registration Required Sept. 23, 2026, 10 a.m. Please register Link downloads document and fill out the event waiver Link downloads document before attending. Enter through the main 1986 Fitness &… Sep 23 Sep\n  23\n\n\n      \n        : NPAW: Coach Visit (Campus Therapy Dog) Sept. 23, 2026, 11 a.m. Sep 24 Sep\n  24\n\n\n      \n        : NPAW: Professional Development Day Sept. 24, 2026, 11 a.m. Topic: Converting academic CV to a resume Sep 25 Sep\n  25\n\n\n      \n        : NPAW: Art Museum  Tour – Registration Required Sept. 25, 2026, 10 a.m. Tours are available at 10 & 11 a.m. There is a 25 person limit for each tour. We Are Here to Guide You Tithi Basu Mallik Assistant Dean for Postdoctoral Affairs Office Phone 609-258-4793 Link opens phone app Email tb9277@princeton.edu Other Resources Princeton Postdoctoral Council Link is external Rules and Procedures Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external Footer Office of the Dean of the Faculty Princeton University 9 Nassau Hall, Princeton, NJ 08544-5264 Phone: 609-258-3020 Fax: 609-258-2168 Contact Us Give Feedback Discrimination/Harassment Complaint Form Link opens in new window Request Data Rules & Procedures of the Faculty Rights, Rules, Responsibilities Link is external University-Wide Policies Link is external Employer Obligation Regarding Records Link downloads document, Link opens in new window Workplace Notices Link is external Diversity & Non-Discrimination Link is external Accessibility Help Link is external © 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University m"
